PG","caption":"Dobroyd Castle","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dobroydcourtyard.JPG","ok_print":false},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Todmorden_Town_Hall.jpg/960px-Todmorden_Town_Hall.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Todmorden_Town_Hall.jpg/500px-Todmorden_Town_Hall.jpg","caption":"Todmorden Town Hall","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Todmorden_Town_Hall.jpg","ok_print":false}],"intro":{"body":"Hebden Bridge is an old mill town in West Yorkshire. It is set in the deep cleft of a heavily wooded steep-sided valley, with a river, Hebden Water, running through it, crossed by the packhorse bridge that gives the town its name. Hebden Bridge has evolved down a wobbly little path all of its own in these parts, and is often likened to Glastonbury; although it is a lot grittier and probably much more deeply alternative and counter-cultural than its southern cousin. Socially, it is home and meeting place for a diverse population, many of them creative and New Age-minded people, with a high proportion of lesbians (and some gay men).","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Hebden Bridge","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Hebden_Bridge","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Hebden Bridge is an old mill town in West Yorkshire. Turf Moor, Bradford City stadium fire and National Science and Media Museum lead its 12 sights. Half a day covers it, ideally in June to August.","short_src":"composed","facts":{"population":4235,"visit_h":3.3}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-turf-moor","name":"Turf Moor","kind":"Landmark","lat":53.78906,"lon":-2.23022,"dist_km":15.2,"rank_score":10.25,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-bradford-city-stadium-fire","name":"Bradford City stadium fire","kind":"Landmark","lat":53.80422,"lon":-1.75902,"dist_km":18.1,"rank_score":7.7,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-national-science-and-media-museum","name":"National Science and Media Museum","kind":"Mus